<div class="sop-template">
  <div class="sop-template-label">E &middot; Scope-creep redirect (mid-proposal)</div>
<pre>Hi {first_name},

Thanks for the note about {requested_addition}. Worth thinking about
honestly so we don't end up with a build that drifts.

Here's the tradeoff: {requested_addition} adds {tradeoff} to the
timeline and budget, and it sits a bit outside the standard plan's
shape. Two ways we can handle it:

1. Add it now as a defined addendum, with the additional time and
   cost spelled out before we sign anything. The work happens in the
   first build pass.
2. Ship the standard plan first, get the site live, then add this as
   a hourly-rate task in month two or three. Lower risk if you want
   to see the site working before committing to the extra scope.

I'd lean toward option 2 unless {requested_addition} is genuinely
required for launch. What's your read?

— Jon</pre>
</div>

